<title>SWEDEN: Trelleborg up on Boliden spin-off rumour.</title>
<headline>Trelleborg up on Boliden spin-off rumour.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swedish metals and mining group Trelleborg AB rallied on the Stockholm Stock Exchange on Wednesday morning, amid recurring rumours that the company would spin off its Boliden mining subsidiary.</p>
<p>&quot;Old speculation that Trelleborg is planning to distribute Boliden (to shareholders) is pushing the price higher,&quot; a trader told Reuters.</p>
<p>At 1010 GMT, the share was up 4.5 percent, or five crowns, at 116 crowns, while the exchange's general index was 0.54 percent higher.</p>
<p>A trader said the share was also gaining ahead of the company presenting its 1996 earnings on February 12.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
